#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:5
#: 8e5f637f49e5433c831e44c4dbbc8274
msgid "Compass Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:7
#: 0d27f2e4dd0044e6bae44f4196bb6ae7
msgid "Operation of fixed wing Planes and some Rovers is possible without the use of a compass (See :ref:`common-compassless`), but utilizing a compass is recommended for all other vehicles unless yaw is provided by some other means (:ref:`common-gps-for-yaw` or :ref:`common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page` or :ref:`common-external-ahrs`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:9
#: eee40f6faa1b4abebd724bcce5de8020
msgid "This article explains how to perform basic compass calibration. It assumes that you have at least one compass, either internally or externally in the system, and it has been enabled. See :ref:`Advanced Compass Setup <common-compass-setup-advanced>` for more information and to setup other compass related features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:11
#: b973926b47f04b80bf7f787a4ee97e1a
msgid "It is important that when compass calibration is done, the vehicle have a good 3D gps lock, in order to assure the best setup. If necessary, move outdoors in order to get a good 3D gps lock before doing the compass calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:15
#: 7e521ca90c8a4f65b6e24842120c1183
msgid "Compass calibration cannot be performed while vehicle is armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:18
#: fa3c2c961dcc420988b4021d26b7546d
msgid "It is not necessary to recalibrate the compass when the vehicle is flown at a new location because ArduPilot includes a \"world magnetic model\" which allows converting the location's magnetic North to true North without recalibrating .  In addition the location's \"inclination\" is calibrated at startup and then again soon after takeoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:21
#: f3f3904e3907412eb237df96c858e89c
msgid "Calibration first steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:24
#: 9ed9a9eb2b67482096be3cc14fed0acc
msgid "Do not calibrate the compasses near any metallic or magnetic field producing object (computers, cell phones, metal desks, power supplies, etc.) or incorrect calibration will occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:27
#: 8a96e81178f34ee6b695518f8d37d9f1
msgid "Under **SETUP\\| Mandatory Hardware** select **Compass**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:32
#: f4a60a44179e4dc08c34a16bf441d0a1
msgid "Mission Planner: Compass Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:34
#: ebc89c10e20542278719e3c695f2b7dc
msgid "You may wish to disable any internal compasses if you are consistently seeing the \"inconsistent compasses\" pre-arm message often and you are sure that the external compass is calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:39
#: a78b000c04ee48e48db4bd43d03ffadf
msgid "Onboard Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:41
#: 5aa1d1fcaed34343b9f5782a2f68b1c9
msgid "\"Onboard Calibration\" is a calibration routine that runs on the autopilot.  This method is more accurate than the older \"Offboard Calibration\" (aka \"Live Calibration\") which runs on the ground station because in addition to offsets, scaling and orientation are also automatically determined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:43
#: 72ac1a927f124317996ee98393956e53
msgid "Calibration could fail for the compasses integrated into the autopilot, if any,  if the :ref:`autopilot board orientation<AHRS_ORIENTATION>` parameter is not correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:45
#: a45625b31f1d4f25bbd8d8b1efc71608
msgid "To perform the onboard calibration of all compasses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:47
#: 5bfe5ad80f914169b44682d6f70669aa
msgid "click the \"Onboard Mag Calibration\" section's \"Start\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:48
#: 43f33b0db27640738680661ca37a347a
msgid "if your autopilot has a buzzer attached you should hear a single tone followed by short beep once per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:49
#: 8f7483686204422590c56b42b18b56d2
msgid "hold the vehicle in the air and rotate it so that each side (front, back, left, right, top and bottom) points down towards the earth for a few seconds in turn. Consider a full 360-degree turn with each turn pointing a different direction of the vehicle to the ground. It will result in 6 full turns plus possibly some additional time and turns to confirm the calibration or retry if it initially does not pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:54
#: 57a601101f13449181a2509b1f4bd68a
msgid "as the vehicle is rotated the green bars should extend further and further to the right until the calibration completes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:55
#: d683a0913cbd4693950787933f88153e
msgid "upon successful completion three rising tones will be emitted and a \"Please reboot the autopilot\" window will appear and you will need to reboot the autopilot before it is possible to arm the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:58
#: 602524a5b4744d558265af24b74c46b7
msgid "If calibration fails:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:60
#: 79c5adb4e7484dbd980c9b116ca45a7f
msgid "you will hear an \"unhappy\" failure tone, the green bars may reset to the left, and the calibration routine may restart (depending upon the ground station). Mission Planner will automatically retry, so continue to rotate the vehicle as instructed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:61
#: 9a54f807373042ea8de5d0c111df2cd1
msgid "if a compass is not calibrating, consider moving to a different area away from magnetic disturbances, and remove electronics from your pockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:62
#: 76ef9f0546794592801ea95cdba400fa
msgid "if, after multiple attempts, the compass has not passed the calibration, Press the \"Cancel\" button and change the \"Fitness\" drop-down to a more relaxed setting and try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:63
#: 9200e11570874dd89bbffc330ae0c397
msgid "if compass calibration still fails it may help to raise :ref:`COMPASS_OFFS_MAX <COMPASS_OFFS_MAX>` from 850 to 2000 or even 3000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:64
#: e1152c6662ec43c3bbb879fc2b56cc78
msgid "finally, if a single compass is not calibrating and you trust the others, disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:67
#: 1386e4e70dec421b8b26140320cb0b9f
msgid "Onboard Calibration using RC Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:69
#: 45b9601e05d04326a821440ef86c4c83
msgid "Onboard Calibration can be started using an RC switch instead using the Mission Planner technique above. This allows calibrating without the tangle of the USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:71
#: 17190e6e633b4035845b360d99739d0d
msgid "Setup an RC channel to start the calibration by setting its ``RCx_OPTION`` to be \"171\". A high value on the channel will start calibrating all compasses and you would move the vehicle as above. A low value will cancel the calibration. The tones for success or failure above will be emitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:76
#: 6ebc86630b1d497882a72bdf79fc4d91
msgid "Large Vehicle MagCal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:78
#: c820564987204afdbf238363a31e06a8
msgid "Large or heavy vehicles are impractical to rotate on all axis. This feature allows a fairly accurate calibration if GPS lock is active on the autopilot and the vehicles actual heading is known, either using a landmark reference on the Mission Planner map, or using another compass (eg cell phone) and entering the vehicles heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:80
#: 89d2985e031c433bab41287b80b4e010
msgid "The proper orientation of the compass must also be set in order for this method to give a good result.  If orientation is incorrect this procedure will appear to succeed while leaving the compass calibration in a very bad state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:82
#: a4e5195f5dd541f398b7a52854fda749
msgid "the heading entered should be TRUE, not MAGNETIC. Using a phone's compass app will usually required adding the local declination value to the reading in order to obtain the TRUE geographic heading which should be entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:85
#: ba4377a002c24772988b7b1314152fd7
msgid "Compass Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:87
#: 2e214cb20aef4c428bc12b7fa6f34e8f
msgid "At the top of the page, you can change the priority of the attached compasses, if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:90
#: 025b1f843610415086f6dfd2b59c2e53
msgid "Additional information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:92
#: 77671f7158fd4f73a98cfb8379b4a7cf
msgid "More information about compass configuration can be found in :ref:`Advanced Compass Setup <common-compass-setup-advanced>`. This includes instructions for how to set up additional compasses, :ref:`automatic setting of offsets<automatic-compass-offset-calibration>`, non-standard compass alignments, :ref:`compassmot <copter:common-compass-setup-advanced_compassmot_compensation_for_interference_from_the_power_wires_escs_and_motors>`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner.rst:94
#: b4b0ed454dab417d9c96bfc4fc622da9
msgid "General discussion on magnetic interference and ways to reduce it can be found in :ref:`Magnetic Interference <common-magnetic-interference>`."
msgstr ""

